        "reason": "The one-sentence statement describes only the error paths (oversized strings, oversized string arrays, deep nesting) of a test suite that exercises the entire cborattr library, which the agent must implement from scratch since the pre-PR package is only a transient link to an absent repository; the tests additionally pin implementation-specific edge-case outcomes that no fair statement could specify without dictating the implementation.",
        "problems": [
            {
                "category": "H",
                "detail": "The tests pin subtle, implementation-specific edge-case behaviors that a different reasonable implementation would handle differently: an integer-array overrun decodes the first element and reports count 1 with CborErrorDataTooLarge, while a string-array overrun that does not fit reports count 0; a text string that exactly fills its buffer is rejected with the buffer left NUL-terminated; an oversized byte string reports length 0. These are choices of how the code was written, not derivable from a fair spec, so they cannot be stated without dictating the implementation."
            },
            {
                "category": "A",
                "detail": "The tests exercise the entire cborattr public API, none of which the statement mentions: cbor_read_flat_attrs/cbor_read_object/cbor_read_array/cbor_read_mbuf_attrs and the cbor_write_* functions, struct cbor_attr_t and its fields (attribute, type, addr.*, dflt, len, nodefault, obj), the CborAttr* type constants, the cbor_out_attr_t/cbor_out_val_t types, and the CBORATTR_STRUCT_OBJECT/CBORATTR_STRUCT_ARRAY/CBORATTR_ATTR_UNNAMED macros."
            },
            {
                "category": "B",
                "detail": "Beyond the bounds/nesting rejection the statement describes, the tests also check the baseline behaviour: successful decoding of text/byte/integer/unsigned/boolean attributes, defaulting, partial decoding, object and object-array decoding, unnamed and substring-key matching, and CBOR encoding. The statement asks for only the error paths of a library whose whole surface the tests cover."
            }
        ],
